      "Abstract": {
        "CopyrightInformation": "Copyright 1999 John Wiley & Sons, Inc.",
        "AbstractText": "A 58-year-old woman developed painful, bilateral ulnar neuropathy in conjunction with small cell lung carcinoma and high serum titer of anti-Hu antibody. An incidental stage I plasma cell dyscrasia, with immunoglobulin G kappa monoclonal protein, was also present. Electropysiological assessment excluded a generalized neuropathy, and nerve biopsy showed marked loss of myelinated and small unmyelinated fibers, without inflammatory changes or amyloid deposition. High titers of circulating anti-Hu antibody can be associated with symptoms resembling a paraneoplastic mononeuropathy."
      },
